$DATUM Boc-γ-Glu[-Glu(OBn)-Gly-OtBu]-OtBu (9). EDC (0.76 g, 3.96 mmol) and HOBt
(0.54 g, 3.96 mmol) and NMM (1.1 mL, 9.90 mmol) were added to an ice-cold
solution of 16 (1.00 g, 3.30 mmol) and HCl.Glu(OBn)-Gly-OtBu (8) (1.28 g,
3.30 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (30 mL). The solution was allowed to stir for 12 h
and was then poured into water (20 mL). The dichloromethane layer was
washed with 10% citric acid solution (25 mL), sat. NaHCO3 solution (2 ×
20 mL) and brine; dried over Na2SO4 and the residue obtained after
evaporation of CH2Cl2 was purified by column chromatography with 50%
EtOAc/hexanes to isolate product as a colorless oil (1.76 g, 84% yield).
R f 0.50 (EtOAc/hexanes, 1:1); [α]D −8.9 (c 1.048, CHCl3); 1H NMR (300
MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.29–7.21 (m, 5H, Ar), 7.49 (s, 1H, NH), 7.19 (d, J = 8.1
Hz, 1H, NH), 5.41 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H, NH), 4.64 (q, J = 8.1, 5.4 Hz, 1H,
α- CH:Glu), 4.14–4.07 (m, 1H, α-CH:Glu), 3.97–3.79 (m, 2H, CH 2:Gly),
2.47–2.41 (m, 2H, γ-CH 2:Glu), 2.36–2.29 (m, 2H, γ-CH 2:Glu), 2.16–2.10
(m, 2H, β-CH 2:Glu), 2.02–1.82 (m, 2H, β-CH 2:Glu), 1.42–1.40 (3s, 27H,
C(CH 3)3); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 173.1, 172.5, 171.6, 171.5, 168.7
(C(=O)), 155.8 (NHC(=O)O), 135.9, 128.6, 128.5, 128.3 (C Ar), 82.1, 79.8
(C(CH3)3), 66.6 (CH2Ph), 53.8, 52.4 (α-C:Glu), 42.2 (CH2:Gly), 32.5, 30.6
(γ-C:Glu), 28.6, 28.3, 28.2 (C(CH3)3), 27.8, 27.1 (β-C:Glu); ESI-HRMS m/z
658.3347 (M+Na)+, C32H49N3O10 + Na+ requires 658.3316.
