$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
(3S,3aS)-3-(aminomethyl)-7-(3-oxomorpholino)-3a,4-dihydrobenzo[b]oxazolo[3,4-d][1,4]oxazin-1(3H)-one
(10a). 9a (3.6 g, 8.01 mmol) was partly dissolved in 60 mL of EtOH and
methylamine alcohol solution (33 wt.% solution in absolute ethanol, 4 mL)
was added. The resulting mixture was refluxed for 5 h and then
concentrated in vacuo. The crude product was used for the following
reaction without further purification.
5-Chloro-N-(((3S,3aS)-1-oxo-7-(3-oxomorpholino)-1,3,3a,4-tetrahydrobenzo[b]oxazolo[3,4-d][1,4]oxazin-3-yl)methyl)-
thiophene-2-carboxamide (11a). The crude amine 10a together with
5-chlorothiophene-2-carboxylic acid (1.56 g, 9.59 mmol), TEA (1.62 g,
16.04 mmol), and HATU (4.56 g, 11.99 mmol) was dissolved in 50 mL of dry
DMF. The resulting solution was stirred for 4 h at room temperature.
Water was added, and it was extracted with ethyl acetate. The organic
phase was washed with saturated NH4Cl solution and brine, dried over
anhydrous Na2SO4, and filtered, and then the filtrate was concentrated in
vacuo. The residue was purified by chromatography on silica gel with
dichloromethane/methanol (30:1) to give 11a. White solid, yield 3.13 g,
84.2% (for two steps). 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 9.00 (t, J = 5.8 Hz,
1H), 7.85 (d, J = 8.7 Hz, 1H), 7.71 (d, J = 4.1 Hz, 1H), 7.21 (d, J = 4.0
Hz, 1H), 7.05 (d, J = 2.3 Hz, 1H), 7.01 (dd, J = 8.7, 2.3 Hz, 1H),
4.63-4.52 (m, 2H), 4.18 (s, 2H), 4.10-4.01 (m, 2H), 3.97-3.92 (m, 2H),
3.73 (t, J = 5.5 Hz, 2H), 3.71-3.66 (m, 2H). 13C NMR (126 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ
166.41, 161.32, 153.74, 144.52, 138.79, 138.05, 133.85, 129.06, 128.70,
122.15, 118.88, 118.81, 114.68, 75.01, 68.18, 66.24, 63.90, 53.42, 49.46,
41.76. MS (ESI) m/z: 486.3 (M + 23)+. HRMS (EI): Anal. Calcd for
C20H18SClN3O6, 463.0605; found, 463.0623.
