$DATUM Boc-γ-Glu[-Hal(γ-bromo)-OAll]-OtBu (54). To a stirred solution of
carboxylic acid 16 (0.54 g, 1.81 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (15 mL) at ambient
temperature was added a solution of the crude amine obtained before (0.39
g, 1.50 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (5 mL), followed by addition of Et3N (0.63 mL,
4.52 mmol) and PyAOP (0.94 g, 1.81 mmol). After stirring the reaction
mixture for 18 h at ambient temperature, the reaction mixture was
quenched with sat. NH4Cl solution (25 mL) and extracted with EtOAc (3 ×
50 mL). The combined organic layers were washed with brine (50 mL), dried
over MgSO4, concentrated and the residue obtained was purified by flash
column chromatograph to afford bromodipeptide 54 (0.62 g, 82% yield) as a
viscous oil. R f 0.40 (EtOAc/hexanes, 2:3); [α]D −11.3 (c 0.86, CHCl3);
1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 6.91 (bd, J = 7.5 Hz, 1H, NH), 5.94–5.81 (m,
1H, CH=CH2), 5.94–5.81 (m, 3H, CH=CH 2, NH), 4.72–4.59 (m, 3H, OCH 2CH,
α-CH:Glu), 4.15–4.04 (m, 1H, α-CH:Hal), 3.41 (t, J = 6.9 Hz, 2H, γ- CH
2:Hal), 2.48–2.10 (m, 5H, β-CH 2:Glu, β-CH 2:Hal, γ-CH AHB:Glu),
1.86–1.78 (m, 1H, γ-CHA H B:Glu); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 172.3, 171.4,
171.2 (C(=O)), 156.1 (NHC(=O)O), 131.5 (CH=CH2), 119.2 (CH=CH2), 82.6,
80.3 (C(CH3)3), 66.5 (OCH2CH), 53.6 (α-C:Glu), 51.7 (α-C:Hal), 35.6
(β-C:Hal), 32.7 (γ-C:Glu), 31.8 (γ- C:Hal), 29.8 (β-C:Glu), 28.6, 28.3
(C(CH3)3); ESI-LRMS m/z 507.2 (M+H)+.
