$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Example 2: Preparation of Trimethobenzamide Hydrochloride (Ia).
3,4,5-Trimethoxybenzoic acid (63.00 kg; 0.29 mol),
N,N-carbonyldiimidazole (CDI 60.65 kg; 0.37 mol), and ethyl acetate (378
L) were added to a flask and heated to a temperature of 50-55 °C for 2 h.
After reaction completion as monitored by TLC, the mixture was cooled to
30-35 °C. 4-Dimethylaminoethoxybenzylamine (63.42 kg; 0.33 mol) (obtained
after removal of toluene by distillation just before use) and potassium
carbonate (41.00 kg; 0.30 mol) were taken in ethyl acetate (378 L) at
25-30 °C under nitrogen atmosphere. A reaction mixture consisting of
N-(3,4,5-trimethoxybenzoyl)imidazole was added to the above reaction
mixture in a dropwise manner so that the temperature is maintained below
10 °C. After completion of addition, the reaction mixture was stirred for
2.5 h until completion of reaction as monitored by TLC. Water (63 L) was
added to the reaction mixture, and the organic layer was separated and
washed with 2% KHSO4 solution (126 L). Layers were separated, and the
organic layer obtained was concentrated under reduced pressure. The
residue was dissolved in acetone (756 L) followed by addition of aqueous
hydrochloric acid (30%) solution (9.45 L). The title compound Ia as a
white solid. Yield: 103 kg, 82%. Purity by HPLC ≥ 99.5%. 1H NMR (DMSO-d
6): δ 2.82 (s, 6H, CH3, CH3), 3.48 (t, 2H, CH2), 3.70 (s, 3H, CH3), 3.82
(s, 6H, CH3, CH3), 4.33 (t, 2H, CH2), 4.42 (d, 2H, CH2), 6.97 (d, 2H, CH,
CH), 7.25-7.29 (m, 4H, CH, CH, CH, CH), 9.01 (br s, 1H, NH), 10.41 (br s,
1H, HCl).13 C NMR (DMSO-d 6): δ 42.08 (CH2), 42.60 (CH3, CH3), 55.05
(CH2), 56.04 (CH3, CH3), 60.03 (CH3), 62.46 (CH2), 104.94 (CH, CH),
114.50 (CH, CH), 128.74 (CH, CH), 129.48 (C), 132.76 (C), 139.88 (C),
152.53 (C, C), 156.40 (C), 165.40 (C). Mass: 424.92, (M + H)+ IR: 3308
cm-1 (-NH stretch), 2957 cm-1 (-C-H aliphatic stretch), 1628 cm-1 (-C=O
stretch) 1582 cm-1 (-C=O-ring stretch), 1236 cm-1 (-C-N-stretch), 1128
cm-1 (-C-O-stretch). Elemental analysis: Calculated: C (59.36%), H
(6.88%), N (6.59%). Obtained: C (59.53%), H (6.79%), N (6.53%). DSC: peak
obtained at 187.65 °C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM optimization study, optimized on coupling conditions and mol equiv of
reagent used in stage 1, 63 kg scale (reactants)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM An Improved Process for Trimethobenzamide Hydrochloride
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Neelakandan, K.; Manikandan, H.; Santosha, N.; Prabhakaran, B.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Process Research & Development (2013), 17(7), 981-984

