$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of 3 (Method C): To a 3-N 500ml flask equipped with
mechanical stirrer was added gemcitabine hydrochloride (20 g, 66.74 mmol)
and 50 ml of mixture of DMF/DMSO (3:1). The reaction mixture was stirred
and NMM (6.75 g, 66.73 mmol), HOBt.mohydrate (9.02 g, 66.75 mmol, 1 eq)
and valproic acid (10.59 g, 73.43 mmol, 1.1 eq) were added in order
followed by EDCI.HCl (16.63 g, 86.75 mmol). The contents were rinsed with
30 ml of mixture of DMF/DMSO (3:1). The thin suspension was heated to
55°C. This clear brown solution was maintained at 55°C for a total of 17
hr. The reaction contents were cooled to room temperature. The reaction
was checked by HPLC ensuring < 4% of starting material present. The
reaction mixture was cooled to 15-20°C and 100 ml of 10% sodium chloride
solution and 50 ml of water are slowly added at <20°C while stirring. The
resulting yellow suspension is extracted with 3 x 100 mL of EtOAc. The
combined organic layers were washed with 2 x 60ml of 20% LiCl solution,
100 ml of saturated sodium bicarbonate solution and saturated sodium
chloride solution (60mL). The organic layer is concentrated in vacuo to
afford 27.10 g of light yellow foam. The purity of crude 3 by HPLC area
is 95.27%. This material was taken on to the formation of the
toluenesulfonic acid salt co-crystal without purification. The free base
obtained above (25.89 g, 66.49 mmol) was dissolved in 50 mL of MeOH and
stirred until all dissolved. The solution was filtered and rinsed with 27
ml of MeOH. The filtrate was added slowly to the solution of
p-toluenesulfonic acid (9.03 g, 46.54 mmol) in 183 mL of water over 50
min. To the resulting suspension was added slowly another 362 mL of water
over 75 min. The white slurry was stirred for 18.5 hr. Then reaction
slurry was filtered and rinsed with 3x70 mL of water. The filter cake is
dried at 50°C in a vacuo oven for 3 day to afford 25.69g of white solid.
Combined yield for the two steps was 80%.
