$DATUM Step 2: Preparation of
(5R)-(-)-3-[3-fluoro-4-(4-morpholinyl)phenyl]-2-oxo-5-
oxazolidinecarboxamide (11) To a flame-dried flask containing
(5R)-3-[3-fluoro-4-(4-morpholinyl)phenyl]-2- oxo-5-oxazolidine carboxylic
acid (250 mg, 0.806 mmol) under nitrogen was added oxalyl chloride (4 mL)
with stirring. The flask was capped with a drying tube, and the mixture
was stirred at room temperature for 15 hours and then concentrated in
vacuo to give the acid chloride intermediate [MS (ESI+) m/z 325 (M+1)
observed for the methyl ester obtained by reaction of the acid chloride
with methanol] which was used without further purification. This
intermediate was then taken up in anhydrous THF (8 mL) under nitrogen,
cooled to 0 °C, and ammonia gas was bubbled in for 5 minutes. The
resulting mixture was capped with a drying tube, stirred at room
temperature for 1 h, and then diluted with water (20 mL) and extracted
with methanol/chloroform (10/90, 2 x 30 mL). The combined organic phase
was dried over anhydrous sodium sulfate and concentrated in vacuo, and
the product mixture was recrystallized from ethyl acetate/hexanes to give
200 mg (80%) of the title compound. mp 185 - 187 °C (decomp.). 1H NMR
(400 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 7.82 (br s, 1H), 7.58 (br s, 1H), 7.54 (br d, J =
15.0 Hz, 1H), 7.23 (m, 1H), 7.05 (t, J = 9.1 Hz, 1H), 5.00 (dd, J = 9.5,
6.0 Hz, 1H), 4.23 (t, J = 9.4 Hz, 1H), 3.94 (dd, J = 9.0, 6.0 Hz, 1H),
3.71 (m, 4H), 2.96 (m, 4H). MS (ESI+) for C14H16FN3O4 m/z 310 (M+1). 13C
NMR (100 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 170.1, 154.5, 153.5, 135.6, 132.8, 119.1, 114.1,
106.6, 69.9, 66.1, 50.6, 47.7. [α]25 D = -23 (c 0.89, DMSO).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
